{"id":"views-wide","window":["2016-10-24","2022-12-30"],"cells_tested":993,"cells_pass_bh":0,"cells_expected_by_chance":49.7,"chance_note":"Expected by chance = 5% of 993 cells at raw p<0.05 (75 seen). Under a global null BH at q=0.10 passes 0 cells with 90% probability.","intro":["Nothing passes. 993 cells were tested across 34 instruments, 3 horizons, classes, years, regimes, terciles and time of day. Against the right benchmark (a random walk with our own vol path, views rebuilt), 0 pass Benjamini-Hochberg at q=0.10. 75 sit at raw p<0.05, against about 50 expected by chance, and the cells are heavily correlated.","The benchmark matters more than any effect. Measured against 0, 11 cells passed, all of them momentum or the combo, negative, in single years or the high-sigma tercile. A driftless random walk produces the same numbers: the one-year momentum IC at 20 sessions is about -0.20 from finite-sample bias alone. That was an artefact, not a reversal.","Combo: 0.00 to +0.01 after the bias adjustment at every horizon from 1 to 40 sessions, in every class. The stage 2 +0.016 sigma a session was the indices' upward drift (always-long earned the same). It is not timing.","Macro-surprise momentum is the only view that is positive almost everywhere. It runs +0.05 at 20 sessions (p 0.03 alone), 24 of 34 instruments are positive after adjustment, and gold is +0.16. But the pooled result is local to 2022 (+0.11, other years about 0), so it is too noisy to tell.","Carry reverses in the FX crosses (IC -0.08 at 20 sessions) and in 2021-22 (-0.15, -0.23), when rate hikes upended the differentials. In the USD majors it is 0.00. Nothing here supports the published carry premium at a daily grain.","Accuracy by vol state: after the bias adjustment, no view reads differently in turbulent versus calm (Lesson 05 regime, 113 per-instrument episodes but only 4 market-wide). 3-month momentum reverses harder in the top sigma tercile (adjusted high-low -0.08, p 0.006), on a plateau across lookbacks of 21-126, but fails BH. Surprise is +0.06 in calm and -0.06 in turbulent, too noisy to tell.","Breadth is real: 163 (view, instrument) bets act like about 51 (N_PR; N_ent 82), and the combo across 34 instruments like 18, while the raw returns act like only 6.5. 27 eigenvalues sit above the Marchenko-Pastur edge, against 1 when shuffled. At an IC of 0.02, IR ~ IC sqrt(breadth) would be about 0.3, but no IC here is distinguishable from 0.","Power: detecting an effect at 20 sessions needs a pooled IC of 0.08 (0.31 for one instrument). What we see is 0.01 for the combo and 0.06 for carry, against the sign we wanted. A published-size view (IC about 0.02-0.05 a month) cannot be confirmed or ruled out with 6 years of data.","As a trade, taking the combo's side at the open (stop 0.5 sigma, on the bid/ask path) beats a random side by +0.008 R [-0.013, +0.027]. Every side loses about 0.09 R net; gross is about +0.01 R. The view is not an entry, a stop or a sizing input on this evidence."],"holds":[{"effect":"combo IC with the next 20 sessions","where":"34 instruments pooled; ~0 in every class (too noisy to tell)","size":"-0.034 [-0.095, +0.022]; minus the random-walk null -0.010 (p 0.7393, fails BH)","benchmark":"random-walk null mean -0.025 (90% -0.065..+0.041); IC needed 0.082"},{"effect":"carry IC with the next 20 sessions","where":"local to FX crosses and 2021-22 (reverses there); 0.00 in USD majors","size":"-0.053 [-0.121, +0.013]; minus the random-walk null -0.061 (p 0.0765, fails BH)","benchmark":"random-walk null mean +0.008 (90% -0.059..+0.062); IC needed 0.097"},{"effect":"surprise IC with the next 20 sessions","where":"positive in 24/34 instruments, but local to 2022 and gold","size":"+0.054 [+0.008, +0.099]; minus the random-walk null +0.051 (p 0.0329, fails BH)","benchmark":"random-walk null mean +0.004 (90% -0.051..+0.063); IC needed 0.066"},{"effect":"mom3 IC with the next 20 sessions","where":"reverses, mostly FX crosses and the high-sigma tercile; plateau k=21-126","size":"-0.084 [-0.148, -0.024]; minus the random-walk null -0.062 (p 0.0483, fails BH)","benchmark":"random-walk null mean -0.022 (90% -0.066..+0.027); IC needed 0.088"},{"effect":"combo: IC turbulent minus calm (next 5 sessions)","where":"Lesson 05 regime, 4 market-wide episodes","size":"-0.067 [-0.135, +0.010]; minus the random-walk null -0.033","benchmark":"label-shift placebo 90% -0.107..+0.045; random-walk null mean -0.034"},{"effect":"carry: IC turbulent minus calm (next 5 sessions)","where":"Lesson 05 regime, 4 market-wide episodes","size":"+0.043 [-0.050, +0.107]; minus the random-walk null +0.028","benchmark":"label-shift placebo 90% -0.077..+0.078; random-walk null mean +0.015"},{"effect":"mom3: IC turbulent minus calm (next 5 sessions)","where":"Lesson 05 regime, 4 market-wide episodes","size":"-0.070 [-0.139, +0.018]; minus the random-walk null +0.011","benchmark":"label-shift placebo 90% -0.127..+0.046; random-walk null mean -0.081"},{"effect":"effective breadth of the daily view book","where":"163 (view, instrument) columns","size":"N_PR 50.88, N_ent 82.17, N_var 86; 27 eigenvalues above MP","benchmark":"time-shuffled: N_PR 147.22; raw returns N_PR 6.53"},{"effect":"combo side minus random side, open race stop 0.5 / target 1.0 sigma","where":"all instruments, bid/ask path","size":"+0.008 R [-0.013, +0.027]; combo side net -0.093 R","benchmark":"random side net -0.101 R"}],"charts":[{"type":"bars","title":"Rank IC of each view with the next 1, 5 and 20 sessions (34 instruments pooled)","unit":"Spearman IC","ref":0,"note":"IC = rank correlation of the view at the open with the return over the next h sessions, per instrument, pooled. 95% date-block bootstrap. Benchmarks: the shifted-view placebo (view moved 1-3 years, 60 draws) and the random-walk null (our own vol path with the returns shuffled in time, views rebuilt, 30 draws). The random-walk null sits BELOW 0 for momentum and the combo: a price-built view against overlapping futur