tle":"Effective breadth of the view book: how many independent bets?","names":["N_PR","N_ent","N_var (90%)"],"unit":"effective bets","note":"N_PR = participation ratio, N_ent = exp(eigenvalue entropy), N_var = eigenvalues needed for 90% of the variance. Benchmark: K (the nominal count) and the time-shuffled book, which is what K unrelated bets would give.","rows":[{"label":"view book (K=163)","values":[50.88,82.17,86]},{"label":"view book, stage-2 10 instruments (K=47)","values":[21.71,30.92,31]},{"label":"combo, 34 instruments (K=34)","values":[17.82,24.19,23]},{"label":"raw returns, 34 instruments (K=34)","values":[6.53,8.94,8]},{"label":"view book shuffled (K=163)","values":[147.22,154.45,135]}]},{"type":"lines","title":"Power: the IC we would need to detect, against the IC we see","unit":"Spearman IC","xlabel":"horizon (sessions)","note":"Needed = 2.8 x standard error (80% power, 5% two-sided). Pooled uses the date-block bootstrap SE of the 34-instrument IC, so cross-instrument correlation is counted; one instrument = 2.8/sqrt(1604/h). Seen = distance of the pooled IC from its random-walk null, either sign. Benchmark: a seen line below the 'needed' line cannot be told from no edge in this window.","series":[{"name":"IC needed (pooled, bootstrap)","points":[[1,0.0227],[2,0.0321],[5,0.0499],[10,0.0664],[20,0.0816]]},{"name":"IC needed (one instrument)","points":[[1,0.0699],[2,0.0989],[5,0.1563],[10,0.2211],[20,0.3127]]},{"name":"|combo IC - random-walk null|","points":[[1,0.005],[2,0.0028],[5,0.004],[10,0.0008],[20,0.0097]]},{"name":"|carry IC - random-walk null|","points":[[1,0.0119],[2,0.0135],[5,0.0315],[10,0.0434],[20,0.0613]]}]},{"type":"groups","title":"Lesson 01 check: every view delayed by one more session","names":["as built","+1 session lag","random-walk null"],"unit":"Spearman IC","note":"Same pooled IC with the view taken one session earlier. Slow views (momentum, carry) should barely change; an effect that vanishes with a 1-day delay would be an alignment artefact. Benchmark: the as-built bar, and the random-walk null mean (what no edge looks like here).","rows":[{"label":"mom1 h=5","values":[-0.0147,-0.0163,-0.0072]},{"label":"mom1 h=20","values":[-0.0567,-0.0576,-0.0125]},{"label":"mom3 h=5","values":[-0.0327,-0.0326,-0.0129]},{"label":"mom3 h=20","values":[-0.0843,-0.0868,-0.0223]},{"label":"mom12 h=5","values":[-0.0181,-0.0157,-0.0308]},{"label":"mom12 h=20","values":[-0.046,-0.0471,-0.0563]},{"label":"carry h=5","values":[-0.0279,-0.0276,0.0036]},{"label":"carry h=20","values":[-0.0534,-0.0531,0.0079]},{"label":"surprise h=5","values":[0.0274,0.0272,0.0027]},{"label":"surprise h=20","values":[0.0545,0.0535,0.0039]},{"label":"combo h=5","values":[-0.0079,-0.0078,-0.0119]},{"label":"combo h=20","values":[-0.0342,-0.036,-0.0245]}]},{"type":"lines","title":"Plateau check 1: momentum IC across lookbacks","unit":"Spearman IC","xlabel":"lookback (sessions)","note":"Pooled IC of log(open_t/open_t-k)/(sigma sqrt k) for k from 10 to 252. A real effect forms a plateau across neighbours; a lone peak at one k is a search artefact. Benchmark: the random-walk null at each k (driftless prices with our vol path, views rebuilt), not 0.","series":[{"name":"mom lookback k, h=5","points":[[10,-0.0147],[21,-0.0147],[42,-0.0284],[63,-0.0327],[126,-0.0378],[189,-0.0373],[252,-0.0181]]},{"name":"mom lookback k, h=20","points":[[10,-0.0275],[21,-0.0567],[42,-0.066],[63,-0.0843],[126,-0.0905],[189,-0.0738],[252,-0.046]]},{"name":"random-walk null, h=5","points":[[10,-0.0027],[21,-0.0072],[42,-0.0075],[63,-0.0129],[126,-0.0201],[189,-0.0259],[252,-0.0308]]},{"name":"random-walk null, h=20","points":[[10,-0.0089],[21,-0.0125],[42,-0.0118],[63,-0.0223],[126,-0.0367],[189,-0.0449],[252,-0.0563]]}]},{"type":"lines","title":"Plateau check 2: IC across horizons 1-40 sessions","unit":"Spearman IC","xlabel":"horizon (sessions)","note":"Pooled IC at each horizon. Benchmark: the combo's random-walk null mean (no edge); the IC needed to detect i